{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7Systems13SystemProfileV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemProfile"}],"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"title":"SystemProfile","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Profiling.swift#L77","fileName":"Profiling.swift"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/init()"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile\/timings"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert a profile into a world to find out where a schedule spends its time. Every schedule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that runs on the world then records each system’s runs in it:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","world.resources.insert(SystemProfile())","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","","let timings = world.resources[SystemProfile.self].timings","print(timings.map(\\.name))","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\"]\"","print(timings.map(\\.runs))","\/\/ Prints \"[2, 2]\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also holds the total, average, longest and latest time of the system’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"runs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A run’s time covers the system’s own work, measured on a continuous clock: not its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conditions, nor the commands it queued, which apply after its wave. A system its conditions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skip doesn’t run, so nothing is recorded for it. Systems in the same wave run at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, so their times can add up to more than the wave took. Insert a new profile to start"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"],"title":"Profiling","generated":true,"anchor":"Profiling"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Resource","doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"title":"SystemTiming","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"title":"Systems","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Resource":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Resource","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Resource","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Resource","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/resource","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that a world can hold a single value of, outside any entity."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Resource","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scheduling Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"abstract":[{"text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile","ident